cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  If you use this app, please cite the work it implements (preferred-citation), this release, and Pennsieve (RRID:SCR_021677); the other works it builds on are listed under references.
type: software
title: cell2location
abstract: Cell-type deconvolution of spot-based spatial transcriptomics (10x Visium) with a single-cell
  RNA-seq reference, using cell2location. Estimates reference cell-type signatures with cell2location's
  negative-binomial regression model, maps them onto every spot of all samples jointly (absolute cell
  abundance per cell type, q05 posterior), labels each spot with its dominant cell type, and finds groups
  of co-located cell types with cell2location's NMF, with per-sample tables and figures.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/cell2location
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- spatial-transcriptomics
- transcriptomics
- genomics
- single-cell
- visium
- deconvolution
- cell-type-mapping
- cell2location
